![Mirror](cover.jpg)

Image: [Wikimedia Commons](https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mirror.jpg)

Say `repo.hex.pm` is blocked at the firewall level in your
organization, or maybe you are somewhere far from the internet with a
poor connection — then an alternative is to use a mirror repository
to install the dependencies.

_Elixir_ allows some environment variables to use another route to
fetch dependencies, if a _hex.pm_ mirror repository has been created
inside the organization.

To use them you simply add an environment variable before running
the `mix` commands.

- `HEX_MIRROR`: For hex.pm.
- `HEX_CDN`: For rebar3.

```sh
$ HEX_MIRROR=https://repo.hex.pm mix deps.get
$ HEX_CDN=https://repo.hex.pm rebar3 update
```

Although the `HEX_MIRROR` variable is deprecated and implementing the
`HEX_TRUSTED_MIRROR` variable is recommended instead. It all depends
on the Elixir and Hex versions you have.

Usage example

```sh
HEX_MIRROR=https://repo.hex.pm \
mix do local.rebar --force, local.hex --force
```

- <https://hexdocs.pm/hex/Mix.Tasks.Hex.Config.html>
- <https://hex.pm/docs/mirrors>
- <https://github.com/elixir-lang/elixir/issues/11414>
- <https://elixirforum.com/t/hex-pm-mirror-for-isolated-environments/24637>
